Version @(#) $Id: ChangeLog.patches,v 1.5 2002/01/23 22:43:27 dl9sau Exp $

020123 Thomas Osterried <dl9sau>

	added comments and my name to the code where changes to the
	original were made - for better reference

020122 Thomas Osterried <dl9sau>

	software like xnet always sends PID=text CText on ax25 connects.
	a connect from wampes to an xnet triggered by an IP frame that
	is routed as AX25.IP VC leaded to a login of the xnet to our
	own system due to the received CText (or to a disconnect if login
	is disabled)
	a modification in ax25.c now fixes this problem with non-protocol-
	compliant hosts like xnet.

020112 Thomas Osterried <dl9sau>

	mail_smtp.c had problems on ax25 smtp (where \r\n is sent as \r\r,
	which results in an empty line.
	additionaly, while profile is running, the cmd.smtp command may
	get lost. now sending \n in a seperate packet before
	issuing cmd.smtp

010213 Thomas Osterried <dl9sau>

        providing patches for wampes-000304:

        I. AX25-tcp-van-jacobsen-compression
                written by Matthias Welwarsky, DG2FEF
                modified by me to be activated with -DAX25_VJCOMP

        II. krnlif.c modification for linux-kernel 2.2 compatibility
            force the old behaviour with -DUSE_OBSOLETE_SOCK_PACKET
